.Dd October 13, 2026
.Dt DIFF 1
.Os ABSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm diff
.Nd compare two bounded regular files
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl u
.Op Fl Fl
.Ar file1 file2
.Sh DESCRIPTION
This adaptation of Toybox 0.8.15 emits unified differences with three context
lines, quoted pathname labels and no timestamps.
Status 0 means equal captured bytes, 1 means different, and 2 means error
or refusal. Partial output on error is not a valid comparison result.
NUL bytes select binary reporting.
.Xr toybox 7
records origin and license.
.Sh LIMITS
Each input is limited to 65536 bytes and 1024 lines. Candidate and traversal
work and cumulative allocation are bounded; difficult inputs may refuse
within those limits. Inputs must be stable during lookup, opening and capture;
this is not an atomic snapshot of concurrent writes.
Standard input, directories, recursion, custom formats, ignore options and
nonregular inputs are refused. Only the displayed syntax is supported.
External process termination is separate from ordinary error status.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cmp 1 ,
.Xr hexdump 1 ,
.Xr toybox 7
